# .npmrc template for @operator/projectkit + @operator/capture-overlay (GitHub Packages)
#
# COPY this to `.npmrc` (which is gitignored) on any machine / CI sandbox that
# needs to INSTALL or PUBLISH the @operator scope from GitHub Packages.
#
# DO NOT commit a real token. The authToken is read from an env var so the file
# itself stays secret-free and safe to template into CI. See
# docs/registry-migration.md for exactly how each sandbox supplies the token.
#
# ── Scope -> registry routing ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the @operator scope goes to GitHub Packages; everything else stays on the
# public npm registry. This is deliberate: it keeps `npm install` fast for the
# public dep tree and only auth-gates the private scope.
@operator:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com

# ── Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub Packages authenticates with a token in the `_authToken` of the registry
# host line. We resolve it from ${NPM_TOKEN} so the file carries no secret.
# The token must have the `read:packages` scope to install, and additionally
# `write:packages` to publish (classic PAT) — or the equivalent fine-grained
# "Packages: read/write" permission.
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}

# always-auth ensures the token is sent even for metadata/tarball GETs that npm
# would otherwise attempt anonymously (anonymous GETs 404 on a private scope).
//npm.pkg.github.com/:always-auth=true
